# File Size Limits

No single source file may grow beyond the limits below. When a file approaches or exceeds its limit, the agent MUST refactor before adding more code.

## Limits

| File Category | Max Lines | Action |
|---------------|-----------|--------|
| `backend/main.py` | 200 | Extract logic to modules |
| `frontend/src/App.tsx` | 150 | Extract to components/pages |
| Any new Python module | 400 | Split into sub-modules |
| Any new React component | 300 | Break into child components |
| Any new TypeScript file | 400 | Split into focused modules |

## Enforcement

1. **Before adding code to ANY file**, check its current line count.
2. If the file is at or above its limit, **extract first, add second.**
3. If you are creating a new file and it will exceed 400 lines, design it as multiple files from the start.
4. **Never make a monolith worse.** If touching a file that already violates limits, extract at least one function/component to its correct module before adding new code.

## Known Violations (must be addressed incrementally)

- `backend/main.py` (194 lines → target 200) — ✅ met (Phases 1–6, 2026-07-14; CORS middleware extracted to `app_lifespan.py`, 2026-07-15)
- `frontend/src/App.tsx` (73 lines → target 150) — ✅ met (Phase 7, 2026-07-14)
- `backend/hod_momo.py` (1226 → 716 lines, 2026-07-15) — Split dataclasses/serialization into `hod_momo_models.py`, pure per-strategy gate evaluation into `hod_momo_filters.py`, and debug-payload formatting into `hod_momo_debug.py` (all <200 lines). `hod_momo.py` remains over 400 lines by design: `backend/tests/test_hod_momo_engine.py` and `test_hod_momo_persist.py` monkeypatch its module-level globals directly (`_configs`, `_master`, `_pending_consolidation`, `_ticker_snaps`, `_cache`, etc.), and several of those globals are *reassigned* (not just mutated) by `load_state()` / `reset_all()` / `_check_and_reset_session()`. Moving the reassigning functions to a different module would leave stale aliases behind and silently break both the test monkeypatches and live config/session resets. Further splitting would require introducing a shared-state module accessed via qualified attribute lookups everywhere — out of scope for a pure structural refactor on live alert logic.
- `backend/strategy/executor.py` (462 → 428 lines, 2026-07-15, Nova OS hardening pass) — Deliberate-flatten logic (`flatten_preview`, `flatten_positions`, IBKR real-position reconciliation, protective-leg cancellation) extracted to `backend/strategy/executor_flatten.py` (151 lines), re-exported as `executor.flatten_preview`/`flatten_positions` so existing callers/tests are unaffected. `executor.py` stays over 400 by design: `_open_positions` and `_kill_switch_tripped` are mutated in place by `arm`/`disarm`/`kill_switch`/`on_signal`/`place_from_ticket`/`_check_fills_once`, and `backend/tests/test_executor.py` monkeypatches those globals directly. Splitting `place_from_ticket`'s gate chain (kill/concurrency/auto_paper/risk/plan checks) or the kill-switch cancel path into another module would fragment a single audited order-safety decision into cross-module state lookups — the every-rejection-leaves-a-receipt guarantee is easier to verify correct in one place. Net effect of this pass is still a reduction versus the 547 lines the safety hardening would have reached unextracted.
